T:Uncle Ev's Barn Dance
%T:The Strut
% NFF Book 2023
S:collected from Con Klippel & the Nariel Band
S:Peter Ellis Collection
B:Peter Ellis, The Waltz, The Polka and All Kinds of Dance Music, 2007, p136
H:Uncle Ev' Barn Dance is known in Australia only in the Upper Murray.
H:The Strut was learned by Ian Johnston from an elderly player from Cobram, Vic.
H:It was briefly used in Nariel, paired with "Uncle Ev's" but subsequently
H:dropped because it did not fit the dance. The Nariel Band also uses
H:"Arthur Byatt's Schottische", "Granma Klipple's Schottische" and "Daddy's Schottische".
H:Source: "Music Makes Me Smile" 2nd Ed, 2015, p182
